                <pb facs="0373" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg285"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dawson to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: This morning the President informed me that
                    he had changed his mind and determined not to make the request, which he has the
                    privilege of making under the award, that the American financial agent take
                    charge of the custom houses at Monte Christi, Sanchez, and Samana.</p>
                <p>He was brought to this decision by the threat of the minister of finance to
                    resign, by the pressure of ex-President Vasquez and other Horacistas, who
                    virtually notified him that they would withdraw their support, and by the fact
                    that Governor Arias at Monte Christi has agreed to the appointment of a
                    Horacista collector in preference to turning the custom house over to Mr.
                    Abbott.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
